# Firebase configuration
# Create a project at https://console.firebase.google.com/ and enable:
#   Authentication (Email/Password), Realtime Database, and Firebase Storage.
# Copy the app-specific .env.example files and fill in your project values:
#   apps/mobile/.env.example  → apps/mobile/.env.local   (EXPO_PUBLIC_* prefix)
#   apps/desktop/.env.example → apps/desktop/.env.local  (VITE_* prefix)

# Shared variable names (prefix differs per app):
# *_FIREBASE_API_KEY
# *_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN
# *_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL   # Required for Realtime Database
# *_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID
# *_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET # Required for blob files (binaries, text > 10k chars)
# *_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID
# *_FIREBASE_APP_ID

# Safe rules rollout (maintainer-owned — see README.md):
#   pnpm firebase:deploy:rules
# Or publish manually in Firebase Console (Storage → Rules, Realtime Database → Rules).
